WEBVTT

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.370
Why did this have to happen to me...?

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.120
Study for the exams?

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:26.080
I don’t need to study, Pinochle.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.000
That’s unacceptable, Freecell.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:32.210
After everything we’ve been 
through, our grades in the red.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:35.510
We need to pull them up by 
doing well in our next exams!

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:38.010
Let’s start studying 
together tomorrow.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.380
I’ll see you at 8:00 at the 
school dorms’ stairwell.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.020
You win!

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:47.460
Is that a bit too early?

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:48.980
Will you be able to wake up?

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.770
Should I pick you up? I think I will!

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:53.530
I swear, you’re as big 
of a worrywart as ever.

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:55.860
I’ll be just fine.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.860
Would you care for a flower?

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:57.990
Really? Then I’ll see you tomorrow.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.530
Yep. See ya.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.740
Would you care for a pretty flower?

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.540
Oh! I think I’ll take one.

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:06.110
Thank you kindly, Mister.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.500
Would you also like a flower?

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:16.170
It’s a pretty flower you could place 
in front of your mother’s grave.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.540
Why is she after me...?

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:31.020
I won’t let you escape!

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.310
Melancholy!

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:10.000
Would You Also Like Some Flowers?

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.630
Here! Have another.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.650
It’s too early to stuff my face!

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:22.130
But who knows when a Master 
Brain will show up?

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:23.630
You’ve gotta keep your strength up!

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:25.970
Good morning, Kaito and Nonoha.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:27.390
Upperclassman Jikukawa?

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:30.810
Guys, why the glum looks 
first thing in the morning?

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.680
Director Rook needs to 
have a word with us.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:34.400
What?

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:46.110
Puzzle Number N927M along 
with V129W and X836Y...

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:51.500
are Puzzles of Fools recorded 
in the POG’s archives.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:58.050
I’ve come to learn that it is highly 
likely that Jin Makata created these puzzles.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:01.420
Whoa, there! Are you for real?

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:02.800
Kaito...

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:04.720
Look, Rook...

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:09.360
Talk about Jin hating puzzles has 
already put me in a foul mood!

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:14.310
Now you’re telling me Jin 
was making Puzzles of Fools?!

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:17.950
There are some things you don’t 
joke about and this is one of them!

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.860
He’s telling the truth, Kaito.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:21.700
What?!

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:26.820
As you’re aware, puzzles contain 
quirks unique to the Givers who make them.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.490
It’s like how you can recognize 
the work of a great artist.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:33.910
I used Iwashimizu to digitalize the 
puzzles Jin Makata has made in the past.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:36.830
When comparing those Puzzles 
of Fools against that data,

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:42.970
I found that there is a 98.73% 
likelihood that the same Giver made them.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:46.220
Jin made Puzzles of Fools...?

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:53.220
In which case, doesn’t Jin Makata 
hate puzzles, just like Raetsel claimed?

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.560
It’s too soon to jump to conclusions.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.980
All three of these Puzzles of Fools

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:01.990
were destroyed by the 
time anyone found them.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:06.280
I believe that Jin destroyed 
them with his own two hands.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.000
What’s up with that?

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:12.160
I, Ana, think he did it 
to avoid hurting anyone.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:17.670
Kaito!

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:22.170
But if he’s gonna trash the 
things, why bother making ’em?

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:28.990
During his blank year, supposedly 
Jin’s skill as a Giver improved dramatically.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:32.180
By creating perilous Puzzles of Fools,

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:35.220
he may have been trying to push himself 
to greater heights and hone his skills.

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:39.940
So he was tryin’ to up his 
game by becoming a Giver?

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:41.690
That logic isn’t lost on me!

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:44.940
Why are you trying to 
sound cool, ex-traitor?

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.440
What was that?!

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:50.780
No matter what, there is no way Jin 
would ever make a Puzzle of Fools!

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:54.030
I’m sure he had his reasons.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:57.180
And they were important enough 
that he was willing to do

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:59.330
that to improve himself as a Giver.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:03.710
No matter what they were, he’d never 
make puzzles meant to hurt others!

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.710
The Jin I knew--

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:08.330
What if he quit being the Jin we knew?

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.100
The Armlet of Orpheus...?

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:15.720
Right. That power devours 
one’s soul, corroding it.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:18.600
It is impossible for anyone to 
defy that power, even Jin...

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:20.030
There is no way!

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:22.140
That would never happen to Jin!

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:25.900
Kaito!

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:42.360
Right. I will annihilate 
all of the puzzlers.

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:44.520
Together with Jin, I will...

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:48.340
You’re... missing something.

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:52.130
For some odd reason, I can’t 
help but get that feeling.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:56.980
Jin...

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:06.230
Freecell? Where are you right now?

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:09.390
A discontinued subway line.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:12.650
Why?! What happened?

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:15.370
I’m being chased by a Master Brain.

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:17.530
A Master Brain...?

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:19.700
As in the one who’ve been 
attacking Kaito and the guys?

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:21.120
Uh-huh. And it’s Mela--

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:24.040
You’ve talked long enough.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.300
Melancholy!

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:30.710
Why are you after me?

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:33.260
Are you truly all that curious?

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:37.220
“As such, Jin Makata 
has my solemn word

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:41.140
“that I will assist in 
annihilating all puzzlers.”

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:43.520
A Master Brain, huh?

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:48.900
As you have been chosen by an 
Armlet, we hold you in high regard.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:54.030
Could you sign my contract 
and lend me your brains?

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:56.900
You’ve failed to pique my interest.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.040
Then allow me to put it another way.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:03.670
Melancholy, wouldn’t you like 
to get revenge on the ones

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:05.790
who’ve taken everything from you?

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.800
Now you have managed 
to pique my interest.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.590
I shall prepare the stage.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:16.050
You’re free to avenge 
yourself however you like.

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:18.430
May I ask a question?

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:19.680
Ask anything.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:24.930
The Master Brains are meant to 
annihilate all puzzlers, correct?

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:25.690
Yeah.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:29.370
Then what will happen to 
all of the Master Brains

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:32.150
once they have run out of targets?

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:34.660
What an insightful question!

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:39.320
Well, I suppose it doesn’t matter.

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:41.450
As long as I enjoy the present, 
nothing else matters.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:47.230
I am willing to accept your 
proposal, M-I-S-T-E-R.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:50.210
Did all of that sink in?

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:53.200
I am the Master Brain, Melancholy.

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:55.220
Please be sure to remember that.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:57.720
I’ve completely dropped puzzles!

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:58.720
Excuse me?

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:00.930
I’m scared of solving puzzles.

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:05.220
I’m afraid that I’ll lose sight 
of myself and go berserk again...

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:06.480
So--

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:08.860
I won’t let you steal 
victory and pack your bags!

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:16.020
Uncle Klondike and I 
have lost everything.

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:23.080
Meanwhile, you’ve cast puzzles aside 
as you try to enjoy a carefree life.

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:25.830
Did you think I’d let that happen?!

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:33.090
I expect you to pay 
for your sins in full.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:41.130
She is absolutely right. I... I...!

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:51.780
Kaito...

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:56.280
Oh, Jin!

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:58.580
What’s up? Did you eat lunch?

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:03.000
Aren’t the Puzzles of Fools dangerous 
puzzles that take human lives?

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.540
I can’t believe I created 
such monstrosities...!

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:10.500
Was I a deplorable person 
in my past after all...?

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:13.000
Jin, you heard us back there?

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:16.420
Maybe it would be for the 
best if I didn’t remem--

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:17.710
That’s not true!

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:29.530
What’s that?

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:32.770
It’s the very first 
puzzle you taught me,

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:35.030
back when I had fallen 
into the pit of despair.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.190
It was simple, yet strong.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:41.650
And... it was a warm puzzle.

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:46.450
This is a puzzle that you made.

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:49.570
There is no way someone who 
could make such a warm puzzle

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:51.040
is a scoundrel, Jin.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:54.710
There is just no way you could 
have made a Puzzle of Fools.

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:56.000
Kaito...

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:02.410
I

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:06.060
know this puzzle...

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:11.060
Who could it be?

00:11:13.390 --> 00:11:15.480
Kaito! It’s me, Pinochle!

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:17.020
What’s wrong?

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:18.860
It’s horrible! They got Freecell!

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:23.370
Freecell is being attacked 
by a Master Brain?!

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:26.370
He’s been chased into 
an underground maze.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:28.370
Pinochle is trying to pinpoint 
Freecell’s location as we speak.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:30.080
Freecell...

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:31.360
Wait a sec.

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:34.460
Why would a Master Brain bother 
goin’ after Freecell?

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:38.550
I think... it’s because Freecell 
is a Phi-Brain child like us!

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:41.370
Then he’s in serious trouble!

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:43.970
He’s given up his Orpheus Ring!

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:45.930
Up against a Master Brain, he won’t...

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:49.800
<i>Iwashimizu! Activate Emergency Code: Q!</i>

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:52.950
<i>Roger! Activating Emergency Code: Q.</i>

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:55.690
<i>Sending an e-mail to “Apple Juice.”</i>

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:57.520
<i>Confirming that he has 
opened the e-mail.</i>

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.610
<i>Obtaining empty seats in economy.</i>

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:03.240
<i>The road to the airport is clear!</i>

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:04.540
Cube?

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:07.850
I have a bunch of backup 
plans on standby just

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:09.780
in case a Master Brain shows up.

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:10.700
Here you go.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:14.230
It’s my new mechanic bug for 
international transmissions.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:17.880
Kaito, I want you to fly 
to England straightaway.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:21.250
If you catch the last flight today, 
you should arrive tomorrow morning.

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:23.760
Take Nonoha and have Gammon tag along.

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:25.340
I’m just tagging along?!

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:27.430
What about you, Cubik?

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:29.090
I’ll stay here at the school.

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:31.850
You need someone to 
protect Jin, don’t you?

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:33.100
Ana, too!

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:35.530
I’ll be fine, so please go.

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:39.230
I would like you to 
stop that Master Brain.

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:42.860
The Master Brains claim that 
they are keeping a pledge

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:44.110
they swore to me.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:48.330
But I cannot let them 
attack your friends!

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:53.550
Didn’t you say that Jin Makata is the

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:56.880
type of person who makes 
strong, kind puzzles?

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:58.550
Huh? Yeah...

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:02.630
I want to reclaim that part of myself.

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:05.340
I’d like to regain my memories

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:07.780
and do everything I can to 
prove that I had nothing

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:09.840
to do with people like 
these Master Brains.

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:15.530
From here on out, that will 
be my personal battle.

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:17.150
So, Kaito,

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:22.900
please solve puzzles 
to save your friends.

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:24.830
Jin...

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:46.300
He actually said to “solve puzzles.”

00:13:46.920 --> 00:13:51.690
Jin, you never once said that to me!

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:13.250
You actually came, guys!

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.050
The way you are now,

00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:19.100
it’d be cruel to make you face 
a Master Brain on your own!

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:21.620
Thank you! I appreciate it.

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:23.300
So, where is Freecell?

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.680
This is where I found 
Freecell’s cellphone.

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:34.220
Going by the trail he left, I 
believe Freecell ran this way.

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:36.180
It really looks like a maze!

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:39.050
This leads to a branch in the 
discontinued subway lines.

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:42.020
But the eastern branch 
heads toward town,

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:43.730
so if the Master Brain 
wants to trap him,

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:46.230
he’ll push Freecell westward 
to keep him isolated.

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:51.450
This path eventually leads 
to an old switchyard.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.400
That is the extent of what 
I was able to find out.

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:57.950
Freecell should still be running...

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:00.410
I’m sure he has just 
about reached his limit.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.910
Kaito, I’m begging 
you! Please save him!

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:05.460
Let’s go!

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:08.630
Hang tight, Freecell!

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:16.010
You’re late.

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:19.970
I had grown tired of waiting.

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:22.310
Melancholy...

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:28.320
Freecell!

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.200
K-Kaito?!

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:35.950
Thank goodness! We managed 
to find Freecell.

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:37.310
Yeah!

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:41.830
If it ain’t Melancho?!

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:45.840
I had a feeling you would 
come, Einstein and Galileo.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:49.500
What is Melancholy doing here?

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:51.090
It couldn’t be...

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:04.940
Are you the Master Brain?!

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:07.060
Yes, that’s right!

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:09.570
Everything went according to plan,

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:12.610
from your coming here down 
to where you’re standing!

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:15.240
Einstein!

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:16.610
Eh?

00:16:16.610 --> 00:16:17.740
Take a few steps to the right.

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:18.620
Huh?

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:19.990
Just go to the right!

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:24.080
Now for Galileo! Take one step forward!

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:26.380
Huh? S-sure.

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:45.060
Kaito!

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:45.940
Freecell!

00:16:56.230 --> 00:16:57.480
What’s this supposed to be?

00:16:57.480 --> 00:17:01.090
The Contact Network. 
It’s a Puzzle of Fools.

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:08.150
Now then, allow me to explain the rules.

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:16.010
This area is five blocks long, five 
blocks wide and five blocks high.

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:18.180
This cube makes the puzzle field.

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:22.470
The players are dispersed 
across Rooms A, B, C and D.

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:25.850
But you don’t know which 
players are in which rooms!

00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:33.070
These are your contact blocks.

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:35.290
Have you noticed that the 
blocks contain pipes that

00:17:35.290 --> 00:17:36.610
extend in three directions?

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:40.620
Link the contact blocks 
to your room and make the

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:43.740
pipe grow until you connect 
with your partner!

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:48.560
Only the two who manage to link up 
will get to escape from this puzzle.

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:53.630
How can we link up when we don’t 
know where our partner is?!

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:56.380
If you connect with a room that 
doesn’t belong to your partner

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:59.810
or if two players place a contact 
block in the same place...

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:05.220
You must connect with your partner.

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:07.960
That is the only way 
to make it out alive.

00:18:08.800 --> 00:18:12.940
But if I do that, I’ll be 
condemning the other two players!

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:16.950
Now then, it’s time I 
selected the fourth player.

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:23.200
If I wanted to torment Freecell, 
I should go with Pinochle.

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:27.650
But using Nonoha Itou to tease 
Kaito Daimon would be great fun!

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:31.850
I’ve made my mind! The 
fourth player will be--

00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:32.860
You.

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:43.560
That hurt!

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:45.890
What is the meaning of this?!

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:47.940
You are going to participate 
in this puzzle.

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:54.030
Melancholy, you are one 
of the Phi-Brain children.

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:58.030
Kaito Daimon with Gammon Sakanoue.

00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:00.180
Freecell with you, Melancholy.

00:19:00.180 --> 00:19:01.410
Those will be our pairings.

00:19:02.110 --> 00:19:04.130
And Melancholy,

00:19:04.130 --> 00:19:07.490
didn’t you say in your explanation 
that this was a Puzzle of Fools?

00:19:07.490 --> 00:19:08.830
You’re such a naughty girl!

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:11.210
You mustn’t disarm the bomb.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:14.460
You may have acted like a villain,

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:17.720
but ultimately, you intended 
to spare them, didn’t you?

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:21.300
I-I don’t know what 
you’re talking about!

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:22.580
Is that right?

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:26.430
I had figured as much and took 
the liberty to rearm the bomb.

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:31.560
Now, go and destroy each 
other, Phi-Brain Children!

00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:35.600
Use this Puzzle of Fools, created 
by none of other than Jin Makata!

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:37.530
Wh-what did you say?!

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:39.070
Commencing setup.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:42.200
This is a Puzzle of Fools made by Jin?!

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:49.710
I know this puzzle...?

00:19:52.660 --> 00:19:53.860
What’s going on?

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:55.630
What are you up to, Enigma?

00:19:56.250 --> 00:20:00.190
I thought I had outsmarted that man, 
but he pulled a fast one on me!

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:02.960
I will not let this slide!

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:06.260
Just kidding!

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:09.640
I was fully aware that he was using me.

00:20:09.970 --> 00:20:12.890
But for him to use me 
as a disposable pawn

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:15.100
when I was raised as tenderly 
as a flower or butterfly...!

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:18.520
Curse that old fart!

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:20.400
Setup: Complete.

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:22.400
Puzzle: Start.

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:29.290
This puzzle is...

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:32.290
I see! So that’s how 
this puzzle works.

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:37.290
This doesn’t make any sense!

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:52.560
I can’t see what my 
next move should be!

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:00.690
I’ll die if I don’t solve this.

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:03.110
In that case, I’ll 
simply have to solve it!

00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:05.900
Sheeit!

00:21:06.350 --> 00:21:09.790
I have no stinkin’ idea 
who is in which room!

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:13.680
What the hell?!

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:16.540
He intentionally trapped himself?

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:19.650
There’s no doubt about it!

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:22.810
Kaito is the only idiot here who’d 
do somethin’ that stupid!

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:25.670
In which case, Kaito is in Room B.

00:21:25.670 --> 00:21:27.980
Melancho and Freecell 
are in Rooms A and C.

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:30.220
Now I know where Kaito is!

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:32.180
All that’s left is 
to connect with him.

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:38.560
But if we link up, it means we’ll 
be condemning the other two!

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:42.570
Would the ever-friendly DaiMORON 
actually wanna see that happen?

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:45.650
He’s givin’ us a message.

00:21:47.820 --> 00:21:50.700
Catch on, Freecell! Melancho!

00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:53.330
There is no doubt in my mind 
that Kaito is in Room B.

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:55.410
But that pattern...

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:58.080
What is Kaito trying to accomplish?

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:00.590
I don’t get it...

00:22:01.230 --> 00:22:04.340
I have no idea which one Freecell is in!

00:22:04.710 --> 00:22:07.170
But I’m not about to give up!

00:22:07.170 --> 00:22:10.100
I will survive this puzzle! I swear it!

00:22:10.630 --> 00:22:13.410
So please notice! Please find me!

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:17.310
Please save me, Freecell!

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:19.940
It’s no use! I don’t 
know where she is!

00:22:21.980 --> 00:22:25.260
Having given up puzzles, 
I’m completely lost...

00:24:03.460 --> 00:24:05.250
Kaito is challenging a Puzzle of Fools?

00:24:05.250 --> 00:24:06.830
Big pinch! Big pinch!

00:24:06.830 --> 00:24:09.340
I’m heading straight for 
England! Wait for me, Kaito!

00:24:09.460 --> 00:24:10.710
Finished searching for a route.

00:24:10.710 --> 00:24:11.590
You will never make it in time.

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:13.090
Don’t try to stop me, Iwashimizu!

00:24:13.380 --> 00:24:16.220
Distance means nothing to me and Kaito!

00:24:16.430 --> 00:24:18.550
Next time, “Farewell Forever.”

00:24:17.160 --> 00:24:26.970
Farewell Forever

00:24:19.100 --> 00:24:20.110
Does not compute.

00:24:20.110 --> 00:24:21.810
You are on leave for the next episode.

00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:23.230
So I don’t get any airtime?

00:24:23.480 --> 00:24:25.690
It-it’s not like I’m 
getting lonesome or anything!

00:24:26.980 --> 00:24:29.990
Let’s try to study some, Freecell!

00:24:26.980 --> 00:24:29.990
Fin Art: Akeru Otsuki
